   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-NZ\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\">\r\n<p></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Hi all,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I am using the “rqss” method in geom_quantile to plot additive quantile regression curves on a variety of plots. In the quantreg package an option is available to plot\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:NimbusRomNo9L-Regu\">confidence bands for the smoothed effects. Is there any way I could plot these same confidence bands on a ggplot?\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:NimbusRomNo9L-Regu\">I have more than 40 graphs to plot and would really like to be able to use ggplots instead of normal R plots.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:NimbusRomNo9L-Regu\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:NimbusRomNo9L-Regu\">Thanks,\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:NimbusRomNo9L-Regu\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:NimbusRomNo9L-Regu\">TM\r\n</span><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<table style=\"BORDER-COLLAPSE:collapse\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"FONT-SIZE:18pt;FONT-FAMILY:Arial;COLOR:#333333\" valign=\"top\"><font style=\"font-family:Calibri;font-size:12pt;color:#1f497d;font-weight:normal\">Theo Mouton</font></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr height=\"2\">\r\n<td height=\"1\"><font style=\"font-family:Calibri;font-size:10pt;color:#1f497d\">Freshwater Research Assistant</font><br>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<table style=\"HEIGHT:1px;BORDER-COLLAPS